.TH RC.CONF 4 "30 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
rc.conf \- which boot services run, and their settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/rc.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B /etc/rc.conf
turns the boot services of the add-on packages on and off and holds their
settings.
The installer creates it, the administrator edits it, and no package owns
it, so installing, updating or removing a package never changes it.
A package can therefore re-create a service's start link in
.B /etc/rc2.d
on every update without turning on a service you turned off.
.PP
Each line is one of:
.TP
.IB service = yes \fR|\fP no
whether
.I service
runs at boot.
.TP
.IB service _ key = value
one setting of
.IR service ,
named in that service's own manual page.
.PP
A line that starts with
.B #
is a comment, and so is the rest of a line from a blank followed by
.BR # .
Blank lines are ignored.
There are no blanks around the
.BR = .
A value may be put in double or single quotes, which are removed; nothing
else in it is interpreted.
When a name is given twice, the last line counts.
.PP
The file is read, never run as a script, so a line in it can do nothing but
give a value.
.SH DEFAULTS
A service that has no line here gets the default its own boot script
names; each service's manual page says which.
A value other than
.B yes
or
.B no
is treated as missing, and the boot log says so.
.SH STOCK SERVICES
Six services of the stock system are installed but do not run unless this
file turns them on; each defaults to
.BR no :
.TP
.B rwalld
.BR rpc.rwalld ,
the network
.BR wall (1M)
server.
.TP
.B rusersd
.BR rpc.rusersd ,
which tells other hosts who is logged in.
.TP
.B sprayd
.BR rpc.sprayd ,
the server for
.BR spray (1M).
.TP
.B mthreads
.BR mthreads ,
the news thread daemon of
.BR /etc/init.d/news .
The rest of that script still runs.
.TP
.B smtpd
.BR smtpd ,
which takes mail from other hosts over SMTP.
Local mail, such as
.BR cron 's
mail to root, is delivered by
.BR /bin/mail
without it.
.TP
.B lpsched
the print service scheduler
.BR lpsched ,
which starts the network printing daemon
.BR lpNet .
.PP
.B rpcbind
starts as before, whatever is set here.
Each is still the stock script in
.BR /etc/init.d ,
with its stock start and stop links; the base package puts a check of
this file in front of it, and the stock stop scripts still run at shutdown.
A change takes effect at the next boot, or when the script is run by hand
with
.BR start .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.ft CW
# /etc/rc.conf
syslogd=yes
display=no        # no graphical login, whatever /etc/display says
ifup_dhcpwait=30  # wait longer for a DHCP lease at boot
swap_add=30       # swap on the slice: 30 MiB in all
ntp=yes           # set the clock from time servers at boot and hourly
lpsched=yes       # the print service, which is off by default
.ft R
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/rc.conf
this file.
.TP
.B /var/adm/rc.log
the boot log, where a bad value is reported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rc.subr (1M),
.BR bootswap (1M),
.BR ntpsync (1M),
.BR display (4),
.BR ifup (1M)
.SH NOTES
Of the stock services in
.BR /etc/rc2.d ,
only the six above read this file; the others start as on the stock
system.
